  # the one-word programs read by their tables: VALS the options that take a value, SELF the options under which the program runs no command or runs it elsewhere and is the command itself, SELFALWAYS the programs that are the command itself and hand on only the texts of TEXTOPT (a text for a shell) or CHTOPT (a command split at blanks), DDONLY the programs whose command stands behind -- alone, SKIP1 a word of the program itself before the command, JOIN the programs whose command words joined are a text for a shell
